  "result": "The 30-minute lesson on O3 is written at `lessons/0001-context-and-memory-in-an-agent.html`. I didn't open it in a browser or count its words. I judged the length from my section plan, so it may run a few minutes short of 30.\n\nIt uses the makerspace assistant throughout and covers:\n- **Context window:** what the model sees on one call, and why a bigger window doesn't mean better answers.\n- **Between steps:** the `messages` list your program resends on every call. A worked token count shows input cost is the sum across calls.\n- **When the window fills:** trimming old tool results, summarizing, and dropping old messages.\n- **Between sessions:** notes as memory, saved by the program and read back at the start of a session or by a tool. Training status should come from a trusted record, not from what a student says.\n- **Retrieval:** chunking the manuals and returning only the few best passages, plus how it fails.\n- **Practice:** a worked \"where does it live?\" example, then one for you to try.\n\nQuiz 0002 (five items) and its key are ready. The lesson also links `cheatsheets/context-and-memory.html`, and I added `RESOURCES.md` and updated `NOTES.md`. Let me know when you want to take the quiz, or ask me anything about the lesson.\n\nThe search tool returned only snippets of the three sources I cite (the Anthropic context-engineering post, the Claude context-windows docs, and Lilian Weng's agent overview), not the full pages. The claims I attribute to them are ones the snippets support, but I haven't read the full text, so a skim of each is worth doing.\n\nI haven't graded quiz 0001 (`s1` and `s2`). Do you want me to do that next?",
